<title>CANADA: Securities body ceases trade in Morrison shares.</title>
<headline>Securities body ceases trade in Morrison shares.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ontario Securities Commission said on Thursday it issued a temporary cease-trade order for shares of Morrison Petroleums Ltd in connection with Canadian 88 Energy Corp's bid for Morrison.</p>
<p>The OSC, Canada's main securities regulator, also said that a hearing into trading in Morrison stock by West Central Capital Corp in the time leading up to the bid would be moved back to Monday from the previously announced Friday.</p>
<p>The commission said that trading in shares of Canadian 88 in connection with bid -- and trading in shares of Morrison by Canadian 88 and West Central -- would be ceased until Friday, February 14, or 48 hours after a decision from the hearing.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
